{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012on1e7ZGHapJ2Dc61j15RD","type":"tool_result","content":"265\t  and its NFKC view, maps the view's matches back, and merges overlapping\n266\t  findings into one span. The output is the original text with only those\n267\t  spans replaced; no normalized character reaches it.\n268\t- The pattern catalog is unchanged.\n269\t- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by Codex and two\n270\t  Claude refuters over several rounds.\n271\t  Codex approved it with one condition, which predates the fix and is\n272\t  declared in Known-open. No sentinel file covers it.\n273\t\n274\t### Fixed — backup and restore\n275\t\n276\t- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n277\t  there is left out.\n278\t- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n279\t  - checks every archive member before extraction (`_restore_archive.py`):\n280\t    no links, no absolute paths, no `..`, no name outside the layout, and\n281\t    never `audit-key` or `.salt`, in any letter case;\n282\t  - resolves `--dest` physically and refuses a link, or a file, as the\n283\t    destination;\n284\t  - refuses a restore target that is a link or sits under one;\n285\t  - runs the same checks in the preview and in the apply.\n286\t- On macOS, the system `tar` adds a hidden AppleDouble member\n287\t  (`._<name>`) for each file or folder with extended attributes, and\n288\t  `ceo-restore.sh` refused every such archive (`archive refused path:\n289\t  ._.`). `ceo-backup.sh` no longer writes these members. For archives\n290\t  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n291\t  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n292\t  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n293\t  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n294\t  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n295\t  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n296\t- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n297\t  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n298\t  `--apply` restores.\n299\t\n300\t### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n301\t\n302\t- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n303\t  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n304\t- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"693e57fe-d263-4dfa-87ac-840e80cc1fae","uuid":"1fdc6341-e37b-4543-8fa5-fd25f0a298b3","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:19:49.431Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  and its NFKC view, maps the view's matches back, and merges overlapping\n  findings into one span. The output is the original text with only those\n  spans replaced; no normalized character reaches it.\n- The pattern catalog is unchanged.\n- The fix is a commit the maintainer signed, after review by Codex and two\n  Claude refuters over several rounds.\n  Codex approved it with one condition, which predates the fix and is\n  declared in Known-open. No sentinel file covers it.\n\n### Fixed — backup and restore\n\n- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n  there is left out.\n- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n  - checks every archive member before extraction (`_restore_archive.py`):\n    no links, no absolute paths, no `..`, no name outside the layout, and\n    never `audit-key` or `.salt`, in any letter case;\n  - resolves `--dest` physically and refuses a link, or a file, as the\n    destination;\n  - refuses a restore target that is a link or sits under one;\n  - runs the same checks in the preview and in the apply.\n- On macOS, the system `tar` adds a hidden AppleDouble member\n  (`._<name>`) for each file or folder with extended attributes, and\n  `ceo-restore.sh` refused every such archive (`archive refused path:\n  ._.`). `ceo-backup.sh` no longer writes these members. For archives\n  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n  `--apply` restores.\n\n### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n\n- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.","numLines":40,"startLine":265,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012on1e7ZGHapJ2Dc61j15RD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
